doc:DescriptiveInformationContentEntity schema1:text "The study proposes a reproducible Machine Learning pipeline tailored to data-scarce urban bus fleet conditions, integrating domain-informed feature engineering, lightweight and interpretable models, SMOGN for imbalance handling, Leave-One-Out Cross-Validation for robust evaluation, and scheduled batch retraining. The pipeline is validated using real-world data from hybrid diesel buses to predict time spent in critical soot accumulation zones of the Diesel Particulate Filter. In Zone 4, the model outperformed the baseline during the production test; in Zone 3, performance deteriorated over time, triggering retraining. The results confirm the pipeline's ability to detect performance drift and support predictive maintenance decisions under evolving operational constraints." .
_:b6f13a34b9f6c6f2a780fa1f506f0e0d rdf:reifies <<( doc:DescriptiveInformationContentEntity schema1:text "The study proposes a reproducible Machine Learning pipeline tailored to data-scarce urban bus fleet conditions, integrating domain-informed feature engineering, lightweight and interpretable models, SMOGN for imbalance handling, Leave-One-Out Cross-Validation for robust evaluation, and scheduled batch retraining. The pipeline is validated using real-world data from hybrid diesel buses to predict time spent in critical soot accumulation zones of the Diesel Particulate Filter. In Zone 4, the model outperformed the baseline during the production test; in Zone 3, performance deteriorated over time, triggering retraining. The results confirm the pipeline's ability to detect performance drift and support predictive maintenance decisions under evolving operational constraints." )>> ;
